<div class="wrap">

<header class="page">
  <h1>TaskFlow API — Webhook Event Catalog</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    This catalog lists every webhook event the TaskFlow platform emits, combining two sources:
    the events declared as subscribable values in the OpenAPI 3.0 specification
    (<code>taskflow_openapi_v2_extract.yaml</code>, API version 2.0.1) and the events actually observed
    in a production delivery log (<code>webhook_delivery_log.json</code>, export dated 2024-03-10).
  </p>
  <p class="meta-line">
    Sources reconciled: OpenAPI spec (declares <strong>10</strong> event values) &middot;
    Production delivery log for webhook <code>301</code> → <code>https://integrations.acme.corp/taskflow/events</code>
    (12 deliveries, <strong>12</strong> unique event types, 11 successful / 1 failed).
  </p>
</header>

<section id="summary">
  <h2>At a glance</h2>
  <div class="summary">
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">12</div><div class="lbl">Total event types documented</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">10</div><div class="lbl">Declared in spec & observed in production</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">2</div><div class="lbl">Observed in production only (not in spec)</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">1</div><div class="lbl">Failed delivery in sample (3 retries)</div></div>
  </div>
  <p class="legend">
    <span class="badge spec-prod">Spec + Production</span> — subscribable via the <code>events</code> array on
    <code>POST /webhooks</code> and confirmed firing in production.
    &nbsp; <span class="badge prod-only">Production only</span> — observed firing in production but
    <em>not</em> declared in the specification's <code>events</code> enum; treat as undocumented until the
    spec is updated (see <a href="#gaps">Known gaps</a>).
  </p>
</section>

<section id="catalog">
