    <dl>
      <dt>Description</dt><dd>Fired when a new task is created in a project.</dd>
      <dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Successful <code>POST /tasks</code>.</dd>
    </dl>
    <pre>{
  "event": "task.created",
  "task_id": 1042,
  "project_id": 12,
  "actor_id": 57
}</pre>
    <p class="obs">Observed in production: delivery <code>d-90001</code>, 2024-03-01T14:22:00Z, HTTP 200.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="event" id="task-updated">
    <header><h3>task.updated</h3><span class="badge spec-prod">Spec + Production</span></header>
    <dl>
      <dt>Description</dt><dd>Fired when one or more fields of an existing task change. The <code>changed_fields</code> array names the fields that were modified, so consumers can react selectively.</dd>
      <dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Successful <code>PUT /tasks/{taskId}</code>, or any other mutation that alters task fields (for example <code>POST /tasks/{taskId}/assign</code>).</dd>
    </dl>
    <pre>{
  "event": "task.updated",
  "task_id": 1042,
  "changed_fields": ["status", "assignee_id"],
  "actor_id": 57
}</pre>
    <p class="obs">Observed in production: delivery <code>d-90002</code>, 2024-03-01T15:05:33Z, HTTP 200.</p>
  </article>

